prompt Petrichor baton lap: read the inner prompt, check the thread and upstream, take a tending target outside the swept docs-geode reach, or close with a log.
think The inner prompt says the Petrichor fruit is landed and its next door waits on Diffuser's Consent Rail, and it says a repeat sweep of docs-geode teaches nothing. The docs/ compressor shelf is the one room this lane tends that no prior lap had graded per page.
think Fast-forwarded one peer log from xy/main (f88460d497, a Patchouli catch-up log that touches no docs-geode byte) on a clean tree before reading.
think Graded fifteen docs/*.md pages with the report card at Door with service 70. Thirteen clear B at Door. docs/CRYPTO.md reads composite 78 at Door, C+.
think The Door reading was the wrong ceiling. docs/CRYPTO.md declares **Style:** Gauge, Field setting in its own header, and I took the flag default rather than the declared setting. Re-graded at --setting field with service 70: register 70 (negative 30 percent of 36 sentences, at the Field ceiling of 30), reach 90 (grade 12 against 11), truth 100 counted, composite 83, B+.
think Door is the stricter setting on register and on reach. A page that clears B at Door therefore clears B at Field for the same claims, so the other fourteen readings stand as B or better at their own declared setting, though I did not check each page's declared setting one by one.
think No page needs a frame. CRYPTO's one soft spot is reach grade 12 against 11 at Field, which is a sentence-length finding and not a red; I did not reword it, since the page holds no load-bearing claim that a reword could improve safely in one lap.
obs The sweep found no repair. Recording the grade is the lap's output, and a lap that grades and finds nothing still leaves a true record.
obs The first Door reading was a grading error on my side, not a defect in the page. The card's own rule says to read the declared setting, and the tool printed qa_setting_agrees=yes only on the Field run, so the disagreement showed up only after I checked it.
rota lap 9354, row 4 -- earth breathes in: took in the compressor shelf page by page, and the one page that read below B was the one whose declared setting I had not yet read.
orbit round 9 sign -- Sagittarius, the mission, in Bhakta, Gauge, Radiant, and Twilight; fire carries the talent, and the lap kept to grading a shelf the lane already owns.
